# ALTERNATE BUILD AND STORE DIRS (NEXT_DIST_DIR / BRIDGE_DATA_DIR).
#
# Tailwind v4 has no content globs — it auto-scans the project and skips what
# .gitignore skips. So a build dir that is NOT ignored is read as SOURCE, and
# its compiled chunks yield class names like
#   [&>*:not(:!<binary>)]:-ml-px
# which fail to parse and take the whole stylesheet down with them. `.next/`
# and `.next-e2e/` were listed one at a time; every new one an experiment
# invented (.next-probe, .next-mobiletest, .next-proddebug) was a fresh way to
# break the build. Match them all.
.next-*/
.data-*/
